## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to design a robust, multi-tenant data export workflow using Azure serverless technologies. It tests understanding of isolation patterns, reliable processing, and production-ready implementation details including testing and CI/CD.

## Key Concepts

- **Durable Functions orchestrations** for long-running, reliable workflow management
- **Cosmos DB partition keys** for multi-tenant isolation (tenantId as partition key)
- **ADLS Gen2** for scalable CSV file storage with hierarchical namespace
- **Idempotent processing** using export request IDs and status tracking to prevent duplicate exports
- **Retry policies** with exponential backoff for handling transient failures
- **Webhook callbacks** for async notification of export completion
- **End-to-end testing** and CI/CD with GitHub Actions and Azure Key Vault for secrets management

## Data Models

```javascript
// ExportRequest (Cosmos DB)
{
  id: "export-guid",
  tenantId: "tenant-123",
  exportParams: { /* user-specified filters */ },
  status: "pending" | "processing" | "completed" | "failed",
  webhookUrl: "https://tenant.com/callback",
  createdAt: "2024-01-15T10:00:00Z",
  completedAt: null,
  retryCount: 0
}
```

## Function Layout

```javascript
// Timer-triggered starter (index.js)
module.exports = async function(context) {
  const client = new DurableFunctionClient();
  await client.startNew("ExportOrchestrator", undefined, { });
};

// Orchestrator (orchestrator.js)
async function* exportOrchestrator(context) {
  const exportRequest = context.df.getInput();

  // Idempotency check
  if (exportRequest.status !== "pending") {
    return { skipped: true, reason: "already processed" };
  }

  // Update status to processing
  yield context.df.callEntity(exportRequest.id, "updateStatus", "processing");

  // Gather tenant data
  const data = yield context.df.callActivity("GatherTenantData", exportRequest);

  // Write CSV to ADLS Gen2
  const blobPath = yield context.df.callActivity("WriteCsvToADLS", { 
    tenantId: exportRequest.tenantId, 
    data 
  });

  // Update status and callback
  yield context.df.callActivity("FinalizeExport", { 
    exportRequestId: exportRequest.id,
    blobPath 
  });

  return { success: true, blobPath };
}

// Activity: Gather data (activities/gatherData.js)
module.exports = async function(context) {
  const { tenantId, exportParams } = context.bindingData;
  const query = "SELECT * FROM c WHERE c.tenantId = @tenantId";
  return await cosmosClient.query({ query, parameters: [{ name: "@tenantId", value: tenantId }] });
};

// Activity: Write CSV (activities/writeCsv.js)
module.exports = async function(context) {
  const { tenantId, data } = context.bindingData;
  const timestamp = Date.now();
  const blobPath = `/exports/${tenantId}/export-${timestamp}.csv`;
  const csvContent = convertToCsv(data);
  await adlsClient.write(blobPath, csvContent);
  return blobPath;
};

// Activity: Webhook callback (activities/callback.js)
module.exports = async function(context) {
  const { webhookUrl, status, blobPath } = context.bindingData;
  await axios.post(webhookUrl, { status, blobPath });
};
```

## Per-Tenant Isolation

- **Partition by tenantId**: All ExportRequests queries use tenantId as the Cosmos DB partition key
- **ADLS path segregation**: CSV files written to tenant-specific directories (/exports/{tenantId}/)
- **Webhook isolation**: Each tenant configures their own callback URL stored in Cosmos

## Idempotent Processing

- Check export status before processing; skip if not "pending"
- Use export request ID as idempotency key
- Implement optimistic concurrency with ETag handling in Cosmos DB

## Reliable Retries

- Use Durable Functions built-in retry policies with exponential backoff
- Store retryCount in Cosmos DB to track attempts
- Dead-letter exports after max retries (e.g., 3 attempts)

## Tests

